Xelian.wikitext:
{{DrukhariPortal}}
'''Xelian''' was a [[Dark Eldar]] [[Archon]], leader of the [[Kabal of the Blades of Desire]]. {{Fn|1}}

==Overview==
A warrior-queen who enjoyed the thrill of combat above all else, she employed large amounts of [[Wych]]es and sparred with them regularly to hone her skills. She undertook large numbers of raids into [[Materium|Realspace]], giving her an abundance of slaves for the grand gladiatorial tournaments she held. Xelian however resented the humiliations subjected to her by [[Asdrubael Vect]] and conspired with [[Nyos Yllithian]] of the [[Kabal of the White Flames]] and [[Kraillach]] of the [[Kabal of the Realm Eternal]] to overthrow Vect by resurrecting the infamous [[El'uriaq]].{{Fn|1a}} 

Vect's agents however staged a false-flag attack on the Kabal of the Realm Eternal's fortress, framing her own forces and drawing her into conflict with Kraillach. Xelian defeated Kriallach during the battle, boosting the reputation of her own Kabal in the process.{{Fn|1c}} But despite this new status, her meetings with El'uriaq proved distressing for the Archon, with the Tyrant of [[Shaa-Dom]] seeing past her facade to her true self: one of bloodlust and mindless violence. El'Uriaq's words on Xelian's true nature threw her into confusion, and later she was killed in a routine training exercise with her Wyches when her bloodlust took hold. Whether she had simply been manipulated by El'Uriaq or [[Daemon|daemonically]] corrupted by him (as had been the case with Kraillach) was unknown.{{Fn|1c}}

Xelian was able to regenerate in [[Haemonculi]] care and was imprisoned in the lair of the [[Coven of the Black Descent]], but this time was possessed by a [[Tzeentchian]] [[Daemon]]. After being freed by Yllithian, she manipulated Yllithian and [[Bellathonis]] into launching a rebellion against Vect, then betrayed and handed in the conspirators to be executed by the Supreme Overlord. However she was killed by the [[Harlequin]] [[Motley]], who revealed her as a Daemon.{{Fn|3}}

==Canon Conflict==
According to [[Codex: Dark Eldar (5th Edition)]], Xelian was male and was involved in the [[Commorragh Raid]] in [[M35]], where the [[Salamanders]] vessel [[Vulkan's Wrath (Battle Barge)|Vulkan's Wrath]] demolished the spire he was standing on.{{Fn|4}}

