{{DarkEldarPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''', the '''Shadow-King''', was a powerful [[Mandrake]] king of [[Aelindrach]].{{Fn|1a}}

Vying for control of Aelindrach against his brother [[Azoruakh]], fortune turned in {{PAGENAME}}s favor when the [[Haemonculus]] [[Bellathonis]] fell into his captivity.{{Fn|1b}} The Haemonculi was able to leverage his abilities to build the Mandrake an army of [[Grotesque]]s, which revealed that {{PAGENAME}} intended to unleash a [[Ur-Ghul]] derived [[Daemon]]ic plague to infect [[Commorragh]] and take control from [[Asdrubael Vect]].{{Fn|1b}} After Azoruakh was assassinated by [[Kheradruakh]], {{PAGENAME}} was the sole ruler of Aelindrach and was poised to invade Commorragh.{{Fn|1c}} {{PAGENAME}} and his Mandrakes alongside Bellathonis were able to use a [[Webway]] gate to enter Commorragh via the lair of the [[Coven of the Black Descent]], where they allied with the [[Archon]] [[Yllithian]].{{Fn|1d}}{{Fn|1e}}

However before {{PAGENAME}}s plan could come to fruition, he was killed by Kheradruakh, who was working on behalf of Vect and was manipulating the rebels to all gather in once place so they could be destroyed.{{Fn|1f}}

