Xin-Myang Khan.wikitext:
{{WhiteScarsPortal}}
'''Xin-Myang Khan''' is a [[Captain]] of the [[White Scars]] [[Chapter]].{{Fn|1a}}

Wishing to avenge the [[Brotherhood (White Scars)|Brotherhood]] of [[Khajog Khan]], Xin-Myang Khan led a force of around fifty White Scars, including the [[Stormseer]] [[Yaghterai]], aboard the [[Strike Cruiser]] ''[[Wings of the Eagle]]'' in pursuit of the [[World Eaters]] [[Chaos Warband|warband]] led by [[Khârn|Khârn the Betrayer]]. The Khan and his [[Space Marine Bike|biker]] Marines were lured into battle on the planet [[Haeleon]], in which they were ambushed by Khârn and his [[Khorne Berzerkers|Berzerkers]] in a narrow canyon.{{Fn|1a}}

As the battle turned against the White Scars, they attempted to evacuate via [[Thunderhawk]]. However, Xin-Myang was wounded by a stray [[Bolt pistol|bolt]] shot and the Thunderhawk was damaged by the remaining Berzerkers' massed gunfire, forcing the gunship to leave the Khan and three of his Marines behind.{{Fn|1a}}

Xin-Myang and his escorts were able to escape the canyon on bikes, but Khârn followed them on a scavenged bike of his own. The Khan attempted to lure Khârn into a sinkhole just beneath the weak surface of Haeleon, but Khârn was able to escape the trap and kill the Khan's remaining warriors. In the ensuing fight between the Khan and the [[Champion of Chaos|Chaos Champion]], Xin-Myang was killed, with Khârn claiming his skull for the [[Khorne|Blood God]].{{Fn|1b}}

