Yarren.wikitext:
{{AstraMilitarumPortal}}
'''Yarren''' is a [[Torathim]] [[Guardsman]] in [[Colonel]] [[Tarvit]]'s [[Regiment]].{{Fn|1}} 
==History==
Before he earned his current rank, Yarren was among the [[Regiment]]'s [[Whiteshields]]. This changed, though, when the [[Colonel]] led them into battle against [[Orks]]. As the two forces fought, Yarren was among a group of Whiteshields that served in [[Imperial Guard Captain|Captain]] [[Murdin]]'s [[Platoon|Three Platoon]]. During the battle, a portion of the [[Xenos]] forces attacked the Platoon and inflicted heavy losses upon it. Murdin was among those who were killed, while [[Commissar]] [[Traidir]] was left mortally wounded. As the Orks made ready to attack their position again, Yarren saw this as a chance to prove himself and become a [[Guardsman]]. However the Whiteshield would need Three Platoon's commanding officer's permission to do so. With Murdin dead, that position fell to the dying Commissar and he agreed to Yarren's request. Traidir died afterwards and Yarren then led his fellow Whiteshields in destroying the Orks.{{Fn|1}} 

Only he and two other [[Whiteshield]]s survived the attack and they were honored in a ceremony after the battle. During the ceremony, [[Colonel]] [[Tarvit]] announced the surviving Whiteshields had earned the right to become [[Guardsmen]]. He then said they would be assigned to the [[Regiment]]'s [[Platoon|One Platoon]], to replace its losses. Also for Yarren's courage and quick thinking, the new Guardsman would [[Warrior Lodge#Torathim Warrior Lodges|join]] the Colonel's '''High Eagle Lodge''', under Tarvit's personal patronage. Afterwards Yarren underwent the [[Torathim]] ritual of manhood for new Guardsmen. This included being given traditional scars, by a fellow Guardsman with one of their world's hunting knives. The [[Adjutant]] [[Morth]] did the honors, while [[Imperial Guard Sergeant|Sergeants]] [[Raddon]] and [[Ferth (Torathim)|Ferth]] rubbed black powder into the wounds, to ensure they scarred well. The two Sergeants then escorted Yarren to his Platoon, as he realized that he was truly a warrior now.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Index Imperialis: Apocrypha]], pgs. 49-51

