Yehzod.wikitext:
{{CSMPortal}}
'''Yehzod''' was a [[Chaos Sorcerer]] allied with [[Chaos Lord|Lord]] [[Vassaago]] of the [[Night Lords]] [[Warband]] [[Prophets of True Night]].{{Fn|1}}

Yehzod aided Vassaago in preparing the planet [[Sarastus]] for new [[Aspirant|recruit]]s from the planet. This was somewhat something of a convenient agenda, however, as Yhezod was more interested in studying a [[Warp]]-phenomenon present on Sarastus called the [[Black Sun]] during each [[True Night]]. Despite this, neither trusted the other (to the point that Vassaago did not consider the Sorcerer a true member of his warband).{{Fn|1}}

Despite nominally being subordinate and master, Yezhod and Vassaago competed for influence over the warband. Vassaago represented the conservative faction that cleaved to [[Konrad Curze]]'s ideal of spurning the Warp, while Yehzod controlled the faction that sought to embrace [[Chaos]]. This played out during the fourth True Night in their proxies within the warband: Vassaago's loyal lieutenant [[Zhara'shan]] and his subordinate, and Yehzod's more fanatical follower [[Haz'thur]]. After the events of this recruiting, with Haz'thur's death and the recruiting of [[Zeth]], momentum in this struggle would start to swing towards Vassaago's secular doctrine.{{Fn|1}}

==Notes==
Although it was said in the short story ''[[Nightfall (Short Story)|Nightfall]]'' that Yehzod claimed that he was a [[Chaos Space Marine|Heretic Astartes]], Vassaago believed that the Sorcerer more closely resembled a fallen [[adept]] of the [[Adeptus Mechanicus]]. His exact nature is therefore unknown.{{Fn|1}}

