Zacherys.wikitext:
{{SpaceMarinesPortal}}
{{Spoiler|source=Renegades (Short Story)}}
'''Zacherys''' was a [[Librarian]] of the [[Avenging Sons]] [[Chapter]], attached to the [[3rd Company (Avenging Sons)|Third Company]].{{Fn|1}}

==History==
When the Third Company was fighting on [[Archimedon]], they were charged with defending a crucial space port.  [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Gessart]], guided by one of Zacherys's visions, decided to destroy the port rather than attempt to secure it and likely die in the process.  Gessart was censured for his actions and the Third Company, including Zacherys, were assigned to a penance patrol.{{Fn|1}}

During the patrol, the Third Company attempted to assist [[Imperial]] authorities on [[Helmabad]] with putting down an anti-Imperial uprising, only to be isolated and slowly ground down.  Zacherys also brought grave news to Gessart: the rebels were trying to open a [[warp rift]].  Faced with the possibility of defeat, followed by death at the hands of [[Daemon|warp denizens]] or further censure, Gessart [[Renegade Space Marine|went rogue]] and forsook the Imperium.  He abandoned Helmabad along with those [[Space Marines]] loyal to him (including Zacherys), leaving the [[system]] aboard the [[Strike Cruiser]] ''[[Vengeful]]'' and set course for the [[Eye of Terror]].{{Fn|1}}

Zacherys was forced to act as the ship's [[Navigator]], opening his mind to the [[Warp]].{{Fn|1}}{{Fn|2}}  This resulted in his partial possession by a Daemon known as [[Messenger]].{{Fn|2}}

==Wargear==
Zacherys's chosen weapon was a [[force sword]].{{Fn|1}}

