Zadakiel.wikitext:
{{DarkAngelsPortal}}
'''Zadakiel''' was the former [[Space Marine Captain|Company Master]] of the [[Dark Angels]] [[Chapter|Chapter's]] [[5th Company (Dark Angels)|Fifth Company]].{{Fn|1}}


==Biography==
At some point Zadakiel fought alongside [[Boreas (Dark Angel)|Boreas]] in the liberation of the Kumenar Gap, and drove back the [[Arch Daemon]] [[Char Gar Kethekon]]. After the battle Boreas gave Zadakiel a special bolt round, inscribed with litanies, cast from metal from the shadow of the [[Imperial Palace]], and blessed by 13 [[Imperial Saints]].{{Fn|3}}

In 949.[[M41]]{{Fn|6}} Zadakiel led the Fifth Company in [[Battle for Honoria|defending]] the planet [[Honoria (Planet)|Honoria]] from the [[Ork]]s of [[Waaagh! Groblonik]].{{Fn|2a}} When [[Warboss]] [[Groblonik]] led its [[Boyz]] in an attack on the capital city, [[Aurelianum]], the Dark Angels responded, intending to break the [[Waaagh!]] by killing its leader. Zadakiel fought a duel with the Warboss and lost; his life was saved by the intervention of [[Interrogator-Chaplain]] [[Puriel]], but the severity of his wounds forced him to enter a [[sus-an coma]].{{Fn|2b}} [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]] [[Balthasar]] assumed command of the Fifth Company in Zadakiel's absence.{{Fn|2c}}

In 961.[[M41]] Zadakiel led 5th company, alongside [[Apothecary]] [[Rephial]], in the [[Pandorax Campaign]] in a cleanup operation.{{Fn|4}}

In 999.[[M41]]{{Fn|5}} During a battle on [[Stern's Rememberance]], he was killed by the [[Hellbrute]] of the [[Crimson Slaughter]] known as [[Mortis Metalikus]] and his position in the 5th Company was succeeded by Master [[Balthasar]].{{Fn|1}}{{Fn|3}}

==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
''Zadakiel'' (from Hebrew for "Righteousness of God" or"Grace of God") is the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zadkiel archangel of freedom, benevolence and mercy].

===Conflicting Sources===

The audio drama The Ascension of Balthasar states that Zadakiel had become master of 5th company sometime after the hunt for [[Attias]] 20 years ago.{{Fn|3}} and the [[Crimson Slaughter]] codex lists the battle on Stern's Rememberance as having taken place in 999.[[M41]]{{Fn|5}}. This is contradicted by the [[Pandorax (Novel)|Pandorax novel]] where Zadakiel leads 5th company in 961.[[M41]]{{Fn|4}} It is also contradicted again by [[The Eye of Ezekiel (Novel)|The Eye of Ezekiel novel]] where Zadakiel leads 5th company{{Fn|2a}} earlier in the timeline in 949.[[M41]]{{Fn|6}}

