Zarha Mancion.wikitext:
{{CollegiaTitanicaPortal}}
'''Zarha Mancion''', known as the '''Crone of Invigilata'''{{Fn|1d}}, was a [[Princeps|Princeps Majoris]] of the [[Legio Invigilata]].{{Fn|1a}} She commanded the [[Imperator Battle Titan]] ''[[Stormherald]]''.{{Fn|1b}}

==Biography==
Zarha was the leader of an Invigilata battle group during the [[Third War for Armageddon]]. Comprised of 19 [[Imperial Titan]]s, the group was ultimately pledged to [[Helsreach Crusade|the defence]] of [[Hive Helsreach]].{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|1b}}

Zarha and her Titans engaged in several prominent battles over the subsequent siege of Helsreach{{Fn|1e}}, although she had to fight ever harder to prevent her will from being subsumed by ''Stormherald's'' [[machine-spirit]].{{Fn|1c}}{{Fn|1f}} She almost failed when ''Stormherald'' got caught in an ork booby trap that buried the Titan under ruined skyscrapers and allowed the orks to try boarding the great machine.{{Fn|1e}}{{Fn|1f}} Ultimately, she was saved only by the intervention of [[Reclusiarch]] [[Merek Grimaldus|Grimaldus]] of the [[Black Templars]], who reminded Zarha of the oath she swore to him to defend Helsreach and pulled her back from the brink of assimilation.{{Fn|1f}}

Zarha was killed in the last days of the siege when ''Stormherald'' was destroyed by the [[Gargant|Ork Gargant]] ''[[Godbreaker]]''.{{Fn|1g}}

==Appearance==
Zarha was 79 years old at the start of the Third War for Armageddon. She spent all of her time on ''Stormherald's'' bridge suspended in a tank full of amniotic fluid with cables connecting her nervous system to the Titan. As a result of the long time she spent near-immobile in the tank, Zarha was blind and her body was hunched and wizened.{{Fn|1b}}

