Zhintas Khan.wikitext:
{{WhiteScarsPortal}}
'''Zhintas Khan''' was a [[White Scars]] [[Space Marine Captain|Khan]], who was among his [[Space Marine Legion|Legion's]] forces that took part in the [[Siege of Terra]].{{Fn|1}}

==Biography==
Near the end of the Siege, he fought to defend the [[Imperial Palace]]'s [[Sanctum Imperialis]], but was among the [[Imperial]] forces left stranded after the closing of the [[Eternity Gate (Imperial)|Eternity Gate]]. Now having no means to escape or receive reinforcements, the remaining Imperials fought on against hordes of [[Traitor Legion]]s, [[Heretics]], [[Mutant]]s and [[Daemons]]. During these battles, Zhintas stood beside the [[Blood Angel]] [[Khotus Meffiel]] and together they destroyed a [[Sons of Horus]] [[Chaos Dreadnought|Dreadnought]]. Afterwards, Meffiel said the Imperials left defending the Imperial Palace, outside of the Eternity Gate had become [[Life-Seller]]s. Their only remaining goal now was to sell their lives dearly and see how many Traitors they could kill before death claimed them.{{Fn|1}}

They later separated and Zhintas' [[White Scars]] would fight the [[Sons of Horus]] again. During this battle, he thought back to [[Khotus Meffiel|Meffiel]]'s remarks and became amused by the name [[Life-Seller]]. However, the concept also filled the [[Space Marine Captain|Khan]] with pride and zeal. With the [[Imperial]]s' deaths now seemingly certain, Zhintas wondered how much his life was worth? The Khan then decided that the forty-five [[Traitor]]s he had killed since the closing of the Eternity Gate were not enough and Zhintas vowed to claim a higher kill tally before he met his end.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[The End and the Death: Volume I (Novel)]] - 3:iv

