|quote = '''''"Competence on the battlefield is a myth. The side that screws up the least wins, its as simple as that."'''<br>- Zyvan.'''''{{Fn|1}}
|}}
[[Lord General]] '''Zyvan''' was a senior officer of the [[Imperial Guard]].{{Fn|1}}

==History==
Zyvan was overall commander in several campaigns that included the [[Valhallan 597th]] and its regimental [[Commissar]], [[Ciaphas Cain]]; these included the campaigns on [[Gravalax]]{{Fn|1}}, [[Adumbria]], and [[Periremunda]]. Zyvan would eventually appoint Cain to his personal staff.{{Fn|1}}

==Character==
[[Ciaphas Cain]] usually demonstrated a wary attitude towards senior officers (since those that weren't incompetent were all too eager to believe in Cain's heroic reputation and assign him to a particularly dangerous mission), but had tremendous respect for Zyvan, considering him an able strategist who demonstrated a commendable concern for the troops under his command (including Cain himself).{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[For the Emperor (Novel)]] - [[Ciaphas Cain: Hero of the Imperium (Omnibus)]], Chapter Seven

